From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:23:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: report per-link station rates and counters

cfg80211_sta_set_mld_sinfo() takes the TX and RX rate of an MLO station
from the link with the least inactive time. The inactive time block before
it has already stored this link's value as the least one when it is, so the
comparison against it never holds after the first link. The first link then
decides alone, and where that link reports no rate the station reports
none.

Since nl80211_dump_station() builds the aggregated message with
nl80211_put_sta_info_common() instead of nl80211_send_station(), a station
dump no longer carries NL80211_ATTR_MLD_ADDR and NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID,
while NL80211_CMD_GET_STATION for one station still does. Userspace that
dumps the stations of an AP MLD can then no longer tell an MLO station from
a legacy one, nor its association link.

sta_set_link_sinfo() converts the last TX rate of a link with
sta_set_rate_info_tx(), which takes the band of a legacy rate from
ieee80211_get_sband(). That function warns on an MLD interface, and the
band it returns is not the band of the link.

mac80211 books the TX bytes and packets of an MLO station on the default
link, because it counts a frame before the driver selects the link, and the
last TX rate there too, because a TX status names no link. A driver that
selects the link can keep these per link and report them from its
link_sta_statistics callback, but it has no way to convert the TX rate it
recorded to the rate info that cfg80211 reports.

When a link of an MLO station is removed,
sta_accumulate_removed_link_stats() adds mac80211's own counters of the
link to rem_link_stats, which then stands for the removed links in the
station totals. mac80211 books the TX of an MLO station on the default link
alone, so a driver that reports the TX counters of each link from
link_sta_statistics, as sta_set_link_sinfo() prefers, makes the totals
wrong at the removal: removing the default link adds the TX of every link
once more, and removing another link drops its TX from the totals, which
then fall.

mac80211 books every frame to an MLO station on the default link, so a per-
link station dump shows all TX bytes, packets and the TX rate on the
association link, and none on the other links, whichever link carried the
frames. Userspace that compares the links of a station, for example to
report the metrics of each affiliated station, then reads wrong values.

